# Enforce LF line endings in the repository regardless of the developer's
# local core.autocrlf setting. Git auto-detects text vs binary; text files
# are stored as LF in the index, binary files are left alone.
#
# Without this file, the Windows default core.autocrlf=true converts text
# files to CRLF on checkout, which can cause `git status` to keep showing
# files as "modified" when an editor or external tool writes them back
# with LF endings.
* text=auto eol=lf
